$DIR/main.p:12:6: second is a second panic handler
    A program has exactly one panic handler, and first (main.p:6) is already
    marked //pu:panic. Remove //pu:panic from all but one of them.
    A kernel has no operating system to fall back on when it panics, so
    Plutonium makes the program choose what happens at compile time, and checks
    the choice: the runtime calls the handler directly, with nothing to
    register, so it works from the first instruction.
    (see "Panics in freestanding programs" in the Plutonium spec, section 17.4)
    (run "pluto explain E2581" for a longer explanation)
